  "comment": "The vectors pinning Prima.Identity: every side derives each public key from its seed, re-signs every entry and request whose signer is named and reproduces its sig byte for byte, reproduces every entry hash, request digest and identifier, walks every chain to its state or to the index and reason it is refused, holds every genesis to its identifier as locate does, and derives each kit's recovery key from its seed. Binary values are unpadded base64url; hashes are sha256:<hex> over JCS bytes; the identifier is per_ and the hex of SHA-256 over the genesis's JCS bytes. A signature covers the JCS bytes of its map without sig. A recover entry carries no sig; its request's signer is named under requests. An entry with signer null was altered after signing or is not signed at all. A locate genesis given as raw is read as those exact bytes, padded with spaces to pad_with_spaces_to when present.",
